            <ArticleTitle>Sudden attacks of head pain in a young child.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>198-201</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In the evaluation of headaches at any age, the clinical features of the episodes are the most important diagnostic information available. In the patient presented, the nature of the headaches suggests the need for further study as well as the most fruitful location in which to look.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
